{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427845-embracing-outside-a-domain","id":1427845,"title":"Embracing Outside a Domain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-09T05:29:25-08:00","id":1427845,"title":"Embracing Outside a Domain","content":"Could a vampire get around the Tradition of Progeny by ghouling their prospective childe, moving into a new city, embracing that prospective childe on the way there, and announcing themself and their childe as new arrivals?<br /> <br /> Perhaps they could spend a few years in some small town where they and their new childe are the only vampires, before moving to a new city so it looks less like they were just moving to skirt the tradition of progeny in case the prince of the new city contacts the prince of the previous city for references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 12-09-2020, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T05:39:10-08:00","id":1427849,"title":"","content":"It would entirely depend on a variety of factors combined - for example, the sire's standing in kindred society (e.g., noteworthy kindred might have trouble with an attempt at a discrete embrace), their clan (the more organised the clan structure, the less likely a discrete embrace would fly), the domain they try to move to (what's the Prince's position on the tradition of progeny, what's their position on the clan of the sire/childe, how much do they need prestation from newcomers, how much to they depend on their primogen/officers for power and thus what are they likely to do about suspect newcomers etc.).<br /> Basically, it's a big old unknown, but it 'could' work in the right circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T06:50:03-08:00","id":1427856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427845-embracing-outside-a-domain#post1427845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a vampire get around the Tradition of Progeny by ghouling their prospective childe, moving into a new city, embracing that prospective childe on the way there, and announcing themself and their childe as new arrivals?<br /> <br /> Perhaps they could spend a few years in some small town where they and their new childe are the only vampires, before moving to a new city so it looks less like they were just moving to skirt the tradition of progeny in case the prince of the new city contacts the prince of the previous city for references.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, with a no. No, with a maybe.<br /> <br /> The thing about the Law of Creation is the fact that it's not actually about the legalese of the Traditions but about summarizing the power of the Prince. The Prince has the authority to determine who will and will not become a vampire in their domain as well as who can or cannot LIVE in said domain. It's not about whether or not you make a vampire in their domain or not, though that can get you both killed,. but whether or not you're showing the proper RESPECT to said Prince by doing so.<br /> <br /> In Lodin's domain, he banned the creation of New Progeny for 30 years and the vampires of Chicago got around that by going to Gary, Indiana in order to Embrace new vampires. This is a deliberate snub to Lodin's authority but not technically against the Traditions. The thing is, Lodin is under no obligation to let you back into the city (though he'd probably be considered harsh for exiling you) and certainly not for letting your childe in.<br /> <br /> Still, it's probably not a Blood Hunt worthy offense either IF you were FAR away and got SOME Prince's permission. If you just show up one day and say, &quot;Oh, I embraced him in Oakland&quot;, then the Prince is entirely within his rights to say you're lying and declare a Blood Hunt.<br /> <br /> Because it's not what you did, but what you can PROVE and sometimes not even then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T06:56:46-08:00","id":1427857,"title":"","content":"So what's stopping Prince A from Contacting Prince B who's domain you violated in embracing someone and seeing how they want it handled? It sets a bad president if you can just go to some other city to fang someone....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T07:10:39-08:00","id":1427858,"title":"","content":"I mean, I've always assumed, since I first started playing VtM back in the 90's, that when a vampire moves to a new city, the first thing the Prince of that city does is pick up the phone and call the Prince of the last city that vampire was in to get information about that vampire. &quot;Hi, what can you tell me about Vampire X and her childe? Oh, she didn't have a childe last year when she was living there? So she must have left your domain and sired a Childe and then moved to mine? Huh. Thank.&quot; Well, obviously it's usually not the two princes on the phone (or writing personal letters) but secretaries, but you know how it is. Ultimately if a vampire causes trouble in one Prince's domain, or snubs a Prince, it's very likely that any other Prince will quickly learn about if that vampire tries to move into their domain.<br /> <br /> Now what would be the Prince's response on hearing that a vampire may have chosen to Embrace a child in a middle spot because they didn't believe that the Prince of their old city would give them permission to embrace, and also apparently they didn't trust that the new Prince they would be living under would give them permission to Embrace either. That just depends on the Prince in question. I imagine most wouldn't particularly care as long as the Childe knows the rules and is respectful. Still, the fact that the Sire went out of their way to sire their child out of sight of the Prince of their previous city might be a topic that comes up in a conversation just to show the new vampire arrivals that the Prince is keeping up on things. Sort of a, &quot;I'm not going to punish you, but I know what you did last summer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course there's always possible complications. Worst case is, maybe the Prince of the first city is incredibly upset and the Prince of the second city owes that guy a boon or they're just old friends and suddenly you and your Childe are staked and in crates being shipped to the first Prince in the back of an 18 wheeler. Very unlikely but, oh fuck, if that's what happens. Maybe the new Prince is just petty and hidebound and takes offense at the way the Prince of the other city was snubbed and (perhaps rightly) wonders whether you will snub him as well? Maybe the new Prince just figures you've got something to hide so he asks some of the more loyal vampires in the city to keep an eye on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-09-2020, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T08:11:29-08:00","id":1427859,"title":"","content":"There is also nothing stopping an Archon from sticking their nose into the situation if multiple domains are involved","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T10:09:39-08:00","id":1427877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427845-embracing-outside-a-domain?p=1427857#post1427857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's stopping Prince A from Contacting Prince B who's domain you violated in embracing someone and seeing how they want it handled? It sets a bad president if you can just go to some other city to fang someone....</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of why it worked with Modius and Lodin is that they were enemies. Even then, Modius was only allowing the Embrace because the young vampires would be allowed in Chicago only after they'd proven worthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427845-embracing-outside-a-domain?p=1427859#post1427859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also nothing stopping an Archon from sticking their nose into the situation if multiple domains are involved</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to guess that most Princes wouldn't think of it as a big deal. If they want to stake someone and their childe for illegal Embrace, the issue is not, &quot;Will the Prince be violating the law?&quot; The issue is, &quot;Who will care if I do it?&quot;<br /> <br /> You only survive in Bloodlines because Nines decides your execution will piss him off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T10:26:00-08:00","id":1427878,"title":"","content":"How would you feel as a Prince when your domain gains a reputation as a place for kindred to vacation embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T11:50:04-08:00","id":1427884,"title":"","content":"Vampires certainly embrace childer outside of traditional domains. The Gangrel, in particular, are known for this.<br /> <br /> However, this isn't an actual loophole.<br /> <br /> Many players seem to think that Princes just allow anyone into their domain. They don't. They can refuse admission to anyone. I think this gets overlooked because the default assumption is &quot;you're a PC so of course you get into the city&quot; and people then apply that to NPCs.<br /> <br /> So a Prince can easily tell the one vampire he is allowed in, but refuse the progeny. Or deny entrance to both. And I think any vampire who seeks to exploit this loophole, probably gets a reputation for this that quickly spreads and he becomes persona non-grata.<br /> <br /> I do think Gangrel are a partial exception to this simply because many of them don't reside in cities, spend a lot of time outside them, and have unique customs on siring new vampires. However, I imagine there are still customs within Clan Gangrel that regulate this to a degree so we don't get absurd situations of a Gangrel siring lots of childer. Gangrel do have gathers, and perhaps there's a tradition of someone or a group of elders making such authorizations. Or if a Gangrel is known semi-inhabitant of a city, he does actually secure permission in advance from that Prince so when he does bring along his new childe the Prince will accept them into his domain. Or perhaps this is devolved onto certain Justicars and Archons who &quot;own&quot; the spaces between domains as representatives of the Inner Circle. In this case an example might be Tyrus of the Wolf Pack who gives such permission around Chicago and other domains of the Great Lakes/Midwest where he operates.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't go into detail about this. But I had the same questions as you when I first started playing. The above is how I handle it in my own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T11:55:18-08:00","id":1427885,"title":"","content":"I think the Gangrel don't have childe overpopulation because they more or less embrace, but leave their childer to watch from afar as we know about them. Some make it through the durance of understanding their vampiric condition themselves, but most either fail horribly where the sire observing them marks them to be a failure and destroys them. It also isn't a crime to do so because of Right of Destruction I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T11:55:24-08:00","id":1427886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427845-embracing-outside-a-domain?p=1427856#post1427856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Lodin's domain, he banned the creation of New Progeny for 30 years and the vampires of Chicago got around that by going to Gary, Indiana in order to Embrace new vampires. This is a deliberate snub to Lodin's authority but not technically against the Traditions. The thing is, Lodin is under no obligation to let you back into the city (though he'd probably be considered harsh for exiling you) and certainly not for letting your childe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. But the situation between Lodin in Chicago and Modius in Gary is strange. We know there was an important Conclave held in which this was discussed, and the agreement forged there articulated many of the domain issues between Lodin and Modius. In general Lodin got what he wanted, but the issue of progeny was an important exception given to Modius. Most likely because the Justicar wanted to hobble Lodin in some way. We're never given the details of that Conclave's decisions so STs can come up with their own. But there's a lot more integration between these two domains then would normally be the case.<br /> <br /> We can easily have the one city allows embrace and the vampire later travels to another between Milwaukee and Chicago. And the same issue applies. Except now we don't have the strange relationship that Chicago and Gary does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T14:26:13-08:00","id":1427904,"title":"","content":"If you find some tiny place with no other kindred and make a go of that, you are basically the Prince there. Go ahead. But you're going to need to spend enough time there to make it plausible. At least a couple of years I'd think. That brings its own issues. Lupines, not a lot of blood supply, boredom. Also, a lot of Princes are leery of granting permanent residence to former Princes of other cities. They tend to be the wrong sort, from the current Princes perspective.<br /> <br /> So you're trading one issue for another. I do wonder however, how many near-autarkis &quot;small Princes&quot; are there? The only kindred in a tiny place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T14:41:27-08:00","id":1427908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427845-embracing-outside-a-domain#post1427845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they could spend a few years in some small town where they and their new childe are the only vampires, before moving to a new city so it looks less like they were just moving to skirt the tradition of progeny in case the prince of the new city contacts the prince of the previous city for references.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is enough if you have the time and strength to survive on your own. Once the Childe has been a vampire for years, he will carry himself like he belongs. If a vampire is going to go across the country to a new city intent on staying, I assume he's already spoken with the prince. Why would you go through the move and not know if you will be welcome when travel has it's own dangers.<br /> <br /> Brujah are another Clan that think little of protocol, so I agree it really depends on the clan. A Tremere might be stuck in a chantry for a decade and then just be introduced as the new member being assigned to that location. I don't see them as being overly sharing with their goings on.<br /> <br /> I would think Ventrue and maybe Toreador would have the hardest time just poping out kids. Nosfuratue are pretty off the radar in the sewer. If you don't plan on taking part in Kindred society in a big city it's not like the Prince knows when a Kindred enters his city with a population of a million or so people. I think this question is very situational.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T16:04:41-08:00","id":1427916,"title":"","content":"I feel like more Princes should engage in torture as a means of displaying their displeasure rather than just Blood Hunts.<br /> <br /> &quot;NOT THE BEES! NOT THE BEES!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://149363654.v2.pressablecdn.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/nicolas-cage-bees.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T16:33:06-08:00","id":1427919,"title":"","content":"Realistically, they probably do. Or a non-physical version of it, such as granting control of choice domains, industries, etc. to the rivals or enemies of someone they want to punish. There has to be some middle ground rather than every offense resulting in exile or death. No one would want to live in the Prince's city otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T16:55:09-08:00","id":1427922,"title":"","content":"I've used public torture/humiliation for lesser offenses that don't warrant death or even exile and appropriate for when the criminal in question isn't heavily tied to a domain or resources. The modern game I used it in did have a public area where anybody could feed (a concession from when the city was a free state), plus the anarchs had a district they'd claimed, so suspending feeding rights would be problematic and difficult to enforce. It's much more the embarrassment of being publicly flogged in court and loss of status than the torture itself that screws with them in the long term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T10:19:03-08:00","id":1428004,"title":"","content":"I would argue, that &quot;fleeing&quot; one Domain to embrace a Childer is not a question of if it is a punishable offence, but if the Prince of the new Domain wants to punish it.<br /> Even without a proper Prince or Domain, the Tradition of Progeny states <i>'Thou shall only Sire another with the permission of thine Elder.' </i>with 'Elder' being the key word. Though most of the people I\u00b4ve met and/or seen argue this, say its up to the Prince to decide, a little minority (at least in my eyes) argues, that it is both a decision of an Elder and the Prince (at least if you\u00b4re part of a Domain).<br /> It gets rather tricky if we also keep the keyword 'thine' in mind. Since most of the Princes would be Elders, one could argue that his permission is enough, while others refer to 'thine' as a member of your Clan. <br /> All this semantics can be a realy interesting scene or even plothook in a game for Players to figure out if they would need to hide their Progeny or not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T22:01:18-08:00","id":1428151,"title":"","content":"Even if you did hide out for a few years in a small town, the Prince would still have the say on whether or not you and your childer can stay in the city when you get back. I'm guessing if you had to hide your childer for awhile it's unlikely they'd let you both back in. The real root issue for reigning in the embrace is for population control. Too many vampires results in competition for domains and risks the masquerade with too many enemic mortals or piles of dead bodies. Maybe your spot's been taken in that time and there's no more room in the city to support more vampires. Letting newcomers in is just as bad as letting a resident embrace, maybe worse, since with a new embrace the prince has some control over who they are and their education. Showing back up with a really nice gift might go a ways, though. Of course the same goes for asking permission to embrace.<br /> <br /> I'd also assume whoever the Primogen for your clan is would also get a say in whether you could embrace someone. It's totally possible if that primogen was at odds with the prince, that the prince might let you embrace just to spite them. Of course if you did that, you'd probably have the primogen as an enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}